29	 The core screen shows the formed state and part count, the reason when the multiblock is not formed, stored power and draw, fertilizer stored, and how full the export blocks are. It lists every planter block with its seed, growing count, module coverage, status and position. Each row has an Outline toggle that shows or hides a glowing outline of that block, for you only, and an Open button that opens the planter block's screen remotely. The server checks that you are within 4 blocks of the core and that the planter block belongs to that core's formed multiblock.
30	 
31	 ## Building rules
32	 
33	 - The multiblock is the core plus every part connected to it face to face, directly or through other parts. Diagonal contact does not connect.
34	 - It needs at least one power block, one export block and one planter block. Fertilizer and frame blocks are optional.
35	 - At most 24 parts, not counting the core. Frames count. The cap is in the server config.
36	 - If the connected parts reach a second core, neither core forms. The core screen names the problem block and its position.
37	 - When the shape breaks, planter blocks stop and every block keeps its contents.
38	 - If a connected part is in an unloaded chunk, the multiblock pauses until the chunk loads, and the core screen says so.
39	+- The core can't tell what is in an unloaded chunk, so a multiblock built against the edge of the loaded area also pauses until the next chunk loads, even when no part is in it.
40	 
41	 ## How a planter block grows
42	 
43	 - Growing seeds G is the smaller of the seed count and the soil count. Seeds past that stay idle.
44	 - One module covers one seed. Module 1 covers the first seeds in the bin and module 2 does the same, so seeds fill both modules first.
45	 - Seeds with the same modules and the same seed data grow as a group. Each seed levels on its own, as it would in its own Powered Planter.
46	 - Growth time, power and fertilizer follow ATE's formulas and are read from ATE's live config. Power is drawn each tick for every seed that is still growing. If the power blocks can't cover a planter block's full draw, its seeds stop growing for that tick. Seeds that are already ready still harvest.
47	 - Fertilizer is taken from the first non-empty slot of the fertilizer blocks. Each tick, planter blocks claim it in position order, and each group claims one item for every one of its seeds or nothing. A group without a claim grows and harvests unfertilized that tick. A claim uses up fertilizer only when its group harvests, so the fertilizer stored speeds up only as many seeds as it can pay for. A paused group keeps claiming each tick, the way a paused Powered Planter keeps its own fertilizer, so planter blocks later in the order can run unfertilized while it waits.
48	 - When there is no room in the export blocks, planter blocks wait. Nothing is voided.
49	 - Breaking a block drops everything it holds.
